@startuml steady-start-writes
!pragma teoz true
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title What a start writes when nothing needs repair: 1 fsync, 2 renames, 1 unlink

participant "main.rs\nProfile::open" as Main #DDEBF7
participant "lock.rs\nInstanceLock::acquire_within" as Lock #DDEBF7
participant "profile::start_up\n(steps 3 to 7)" as Start #DDEBF7
participant "gaze-fs\nreplace_unsynced" as Fs #DDEBF7
participant "the kernel\n(ext4, data=ordered)" as Kernel #E2EFDA

== The instance lock (section 8) ==
Main -> Lock : acquire
Lock -> Kernel : open data/instance.lock (O_RDWR | O_CREAT); flock (LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB)
Lock -> Kernel : open runtime/instance.lock; flock; fchmod 01600 (sticky, Linux)
Lock -> Kernel : data/instance.lock: ftruncate, write (pid, mode, start time)
Lock -> Fs : data/instance.pid (the holder, for readers on Windows)
Fs -> Kernel : create .instance.pid.tmp-<pid>-0, write
Fs -> Kernel : rename over instance.pid
Lock -> Kernel : runtime/instance.lock: ftruncate, write
Lock -> Fs : runtime/instance.pid, the same
Fs -> Kernel : create, write; rename
note right of Fs #EDEDED
  not synced: a crash ends the hold
  the record names (V1, ledger S15
  parts 2 and 3: 4 fsyncs, 0.35 ms
  less a start); readers never see
  half of it
end note

== Start-up (section 9.1) ==
Main -> Start : start_up
Start -> Kernel : step 3: create data/.startup-busy (empty, not synced);\nthe marker is there and no flag was: no barrier
Start -> Kernel : steps 4 to 6: the layout's marker, the skeleton,\nthe sweeps and every managed file: read only
note right of Kernel #EDEDED
  a profile that needs nothing
  makes no other write
end note
Start -> Kernel : step 7: unlink data/.startup-busy
Start -> Kernel : **fsync** data/: the next start needs no barrier
note right of Kernel #FCE4D6
  each fsync commits ext4's journal;
  another program's flush can hold
  a commit for up to about 50 ms (H-out'')
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#DDEBF7> | F1R3Gaze code |
  |<#E2EFDA> | the operating system |
  |<#FCE4D6> | durability points: what an fsync costs |
  |<#EDEDED> | reads, which write nothing |
endlegend
@enduml
